WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.116 --> 00:00:02.046
- What even is mince meat

00:00:02.046 --> 00:00:04.260
and why would we want to put it in a pie?

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:09.061
(guitar christmas music)

00:00:15.496 --> 00:00:16.735
- I hope it's not liver.

00:00:16.735 --> 00:00:18.415
- It's made of mince.

00:00:18.415 --> 00:00:19.532
- [Man] And what's mince?

00:00:19.532 --> 00:00:21.663
- I have no idea.

00:00:22.774 --> 00:00:23.689
- Oh boy.

00:00:23.689 --> 00:00:25.111
- This has some nice weight to it.

00:00:25.111 --> 00:00:27.935
- The crust looks nicely done.

00:00:27.935 --> 00:00:30.007
- I like the little
sugar sprinkles on top.

00:00:30.007 --> 00:00:32.242
- It has three holes in the top.

00:00:32.242 --> 00:00:33.888
- I don't even know how to
get it out of the container.

00:00:33.888 --> 00:00:36.448
- We don't want to litter up our whiskers

00:00:36.448 --> 00:00:39.130
with a bunch of pie crust.

00:00:39.130 --> 00:00:41.452
- First time ever.

00:00:42.076 --> 00:00:43.295
- Now that's interesting.

00:00:43.295 --> 00:00:44.229
- The crust is good.

00:00:44.229 --> 00:00:45.611
- Chewy.

00:00:45.611 --> 00:00:47.602
- Tasty but it's dry.

00:00:47.602 --> 00:00:50.243
- The top of the crust is
very crumbly, very good.

00:00:50.243 --> 00:00:52.498
- Raisins and I'm not sure, some cinnamon.

00:00:52.498 --> 00:00:54.611
- I'm enjoying the taste

00:00:54.611 --> 00:00:55.830
and the sensation

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:57.374
and the texture.

00:00:57.374 --> 00:00:59.447
- You know it tastes a little bit raisiny.

00:00:59.447 --> 00:01:01.397
- But you need something
to drink with this.

00:01:01.397 --> 00:01:02.555
Maybe some hot chocolate

00:01:02.555 --> 00:01:04.079
or some hot tea.

00:01:04.079 --> 00:01:06.015
- What the hay?

00:01:06.415 --> 00:01:09.382
- That reminds me a Thanksgiving pie that

00:01:09.382 --> 00:01:11.587
my mother used to make
years and years ago.

00:01:11.587 --> 00:01:12.907
- I would revisit these.

00:01:12.907 --> 00:01:15.305
- This is a treat that
we have to teach more

00:01:15.305 --> 00:01:17.763
American households to make I think.

00:01:17.763 --> 00:01:19.948
- This was an excellent pie.

00:01:19.948 --> 00:01:23.666
- Don't look at something and
say ew, ick, I don't like it.

00:01:23.666 --> 00:01:24.784
Try it.

00:01:24.784 --> 00:01:26.685
- Very good, very well done.

00:01:26.685 --> 00:01:30.179
- So if you're thinking of
putting out something for Santa,

00:01:30.179 --> 00:01:31.601
a little mince pie.

00:01:31.601 --> 00:01:32.902
(Santa laughing)

00:01:32.902 --> 00:01:34.854
I love it, thank you.

